      ":question/id": "3f5e6ecc-399e-5485-8fbc-8859883424b5",
      ":question/problem": "$\\int \\frac{1}{1-4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=1-4x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u$, solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1-4x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
